.TH mnnn-mcp-serve 1  "mnnn-mcp-serve 2.25.0" 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
mnnn\-mcp\-serve \- Serve Muninn over MCP: stdio for one client (`\-\-client NAME`), or HTTP (`\-\-http`)
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmnnn mcp serve\fR [\fB\-\-client\fR] [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-\-db\fR] [\fB\-\-http\fR] [\fB\-\-non\-interactive\fR] [\fB\-\-tls\-domain\fR] [\fB\-\-tls\-email\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-\-log\-file\fR] [\fB\-\-tls\-cert\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-tls\-key\fR] [\fB\-\-acme\-staging\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-acme\-directory\fR] [\fB\-\-theme\-mode\fR] [\fB\-\-acme\-challenge\fR] [\fB\-\-transport\fR] [\fB\-\-acme\-http\-port\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
Serve Muninn over MCP: stdio for one client (`\-\-client NAME`), or HTTP (`\-\-http`)
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-client\fR \fI<CLIENT>\fR
The client to serve over stdio (see `mnnn mcp client add`)
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Muninn home directory (default ~/.muninn)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_HOME\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-db\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Database file (default <home>/storage/muninn.database)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_DB\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-http\fR [\fI<ADDR>\fR]
Serve over HTTP instead, at ADDR (default 127.0.0.1:4743, or 0.0.0.0:443 with TLS; `[mcp] bind`); clients send their token
.TP
\fB\-\-non\-interactive\fR
Never prompt; missing values are errors
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_NON_INTERACTIVE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-tls\-domain\fR \fI<DOMAIN>\fR
Serve HTTPS with a Let\*(Aqs Encrypt certificate for DOMAIN, got and renewed while running (`[mcp.acme] domain`). It must point at this machine
.TP
\fB\-\-tls\-email\fR \fI<EMAIL>\fR
Contact address given to the CA (default `[mcp.acme] email`, else `[hosting.acme] email`)
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
More output (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-file\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Write logs to this file instead of stderr (the TUI defaults to <home>/logs/tui.log)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_LOG_FILE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-tls\-cert\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Serve HTTPS with your own certificate chain (PEM; with \-\-tls\-key, no renewal)
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Print nothing but errors and requested data
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_QUIET\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-tls\-key\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
The key for \-\-tls\-cert (PEM)
.TP
\fB\-\-acme\-staging\fR
Use Let\*(Aqs Encrypt\*(Aqs staging CA (untrusted certificates, for trying it out)
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Answer yes to every confirmation
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_YES\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-acme\-directory\fR \fI<URL>\fR
letsencrypt, letsencrypt\-staging or a directory URL (`[mcp.acme] directory`)
.TP
\fB\-\-theme\-mode\fR \fI<THEME_MODE>\fR
Override the theme mode for this run
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
light
.IP \(bu 2
dark
.IP \(bu 2
system
.RE
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_THEME_MODE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-acme\-challenge\fR \fI<CHALLENGE>\fR
http\-01 (port 80 reaches \-\-acme\-http\-port) or tls\-alpn\-01 (443 reaches the server)
.TP
\fB\-\-transport\fR \fI<stream|poll>\fR
How live collaboration reaches peers: `stream` (gRPC streams, the default) or `poll` (requests over the peer connection; for containers). Overrides MUNINN_COLLAB_TRANSPORT and the `net config \-\-collab\-transport` setting
.TP
\fB\-\-acme\-http\-port\fR \fI<PORT>\fR
Port the HTTP\-01 challenge is answered on (default 80)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
